# This directory is watched by cargo through the build script's
# `rerun-if-changed` directive (tauri-build emits it for the capabilities
# path). Cargo re-runs a build script on every build when a watched path is
# missing, and the rewritten build output then marks the app crate stale, so
# the shell was recompiled - twelve seconds - on every single launch.
#
# The file itself only has to exist: Project KO's interface talks to its own
# service over HTTP and never uses the Tauri JavaScript API, so it needs no
# capabilities. Keeping the directory means cargo has something stable to
# watch, and the build script stays fresh.
